// grades.fluid: a small program that fx3c 0.1 can build completely.
// Try it:   fluidc run examples/grades.fluid

app Grade Book
    Keep students' marks and print a report card for the class.

target python

settings
    pass mark is 40
    top grade needs 90

words
    "average"   the mean of a student's marks, rounded to 1 decimal place

thing Student
    name: text
    marks: a list of whole numbers from 0 to 100

to average of (student) -> a number
    The "average" of the student's marks. A student with no marks has average 0.

    example
        Student "Ria" with marks 80, 90 -> 85.0

check grade for (average)
    at least the top grade   -> A
    at least 75              -> B
    at least the pass mark   -> C
    otherwise                -> F

to class report (students)
    Print one line per student: name, average, grade.
    Then print how many passed (a grade that is not F).

rules
    marks are always between 0 and 100
    the report never shows a student twice       [warn]

test top student gets an A
    a student with marks 95 and 92 -> grade A

on start
    Build a class of Sam (95, 88), Ria (72, 65, 80) and Tom (30, 45), and print the class report.
